====================================================================================================
[FINDING] 3.4: 'at least 0.088 L sqrt(K/n) unfaithful calls' is printed without the range n >= K/2 of the proof file; for n < 0.0078 K it exceeds the number L of calls
       K = 1000, L = 10, n = 5: 0.088 L sqrt(K/n) = 12.45 > L = 10
[FINDING] 4.6 N2d(a): printed without a range for delta; for delta > 1/4 the bound 4F/(1 - 4 delta) on r L/n is negative
       delta = 0.3, r = 1: 4F/(1-4 delta) = -6.0
[FINDING] 3.1 'It is empty for n below L K ln 2': the bound on the expected number of unfaithful calls is below the trivial L as soon as n > K ln 2
       L = 10, K = 100, n = 80 < L K ln2 = 693: the bound says 8.7 of 10 calls; it is empty only as a bound on the probability that a run has an unfaithful call
[FINDING] 13 item 3 'K + 3 disagreements ... and log2(1/pi(B)) + 2 violations': with the halved weights of 8.4 the second number is log2(1/pi(B)) + 3 in the original weights
[PASS] N2 at L = 1, delta = 1/6 (N = 3): the three lower bounds 0, 0.5 and 1 are consistent with what is achievable
       exact inequality gives n >= 1; a mixture of 1 and 2 non-adaptive questions (expected 1.5) reaches failure 1/6: 0.5*(2/9) + 0.5*(1/9) = 0.1667
[PASS] N5 with k = 0 is N2 (integer case) with L = g; N8 with k = 0 is N2b with L = g
[PASS] R4 with L = 1 has the constant of R1: 2L^2/(L+1) = 1
[PASS] V1(a): for m <= ln(1/delta) the certified bound L ln(1/delta)/m is at least L (true and empty)
[PASS] N3 at a = 1/2 (deployed answer always right): n >= N, one question in every region
[PASS] H1 with N = 1: the bound K ln 2 is the divergence from the prior mixture, which is at most ln(1/w(P))

